            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>The magicircuitry patterns etched on the surface of each Starstone guardian's body are unique. They tell the story of each guardian's creation ritual. Though incredibly ancient, the magic that sustains the Starstone guardians refreshes and restores them over time, making Starstone guardians effectively immortal. These constructs often become uncomfortable if addressed as if they're distinct individuals. If asked for a designation, each insists they are to be referred to simply as \"Guardian.\"</p>\n<p>More powerful iterations of the guardians were created to protect the reactor's network of facilities, called the prime virtues by the engineers and historians who study them. With few exceptions, the prime virtues are rarely encountered by ordinary people. All have unique features and personalities that make such experiences unforgettable, and sometimes dangerous. The characteristics and capabilities of the prime virtues aren't well understood for this reason.</p>\n<p>Starstone guardians are peaceful when they aren't deployed to protect the reactor network keeping the entire space station spinning, but their defenses aren't infallible. Corrupted or controlled Starstone guardians are more likely to attack.</p><h2>STARSTONE CONSTRUCTS</h2><p>Starstone constructs are ancient magitech constructs that serve to protect and maintain the Starstone reactor, the station's power source fueled by the legendary Starstone. They are reticent and standoffish creatures whose sole area of concern is the reactor and its continued functionality. Starstone constructs are vigilant and pious, performing their duties with unmistakable reverence. They are almost never seen outside of the Spike, and only rarely outside the chambers around the Starstone reactor. They attempt to complete whatever tasks take them away from their primary focus quickly and efficiently.</p>\n<p>Starstone constructs are tall, broad-shouldered robotic humanoids of gleaming platinum with slender limbs made of a translucent blue crystal. Their faces are mask-like and nearly featureless but for three circular eye holes containing luminous spheres that blink, widen, narrow, and otherwise move like a biological creature's eyes. Each Starstone construct has a pattern of intricate magicircuitry etched into their crystalline limbs and down the sides of their metallic torso.</p>\n<p>Starstone constructs have humanlike forms but don't follow most humanoid customs and habits, except for a custom of adorning themselves with cloth drapery, similar to how a humanoid would wear clothing. Starstone stoles are embroidered with spelled thread and are believed to contain immense magical energy.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
        },
